--
--   Description
-- 
-- Tests the events that cause the statistics registers to increment during 
-- gigabit operation in burst mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- � Check that various events are recorded in the stats registers.
-- � Ensure proper operation of crs (carrier sense) bit.
-- � Ensure proper checking of crc errors in received 
--     frames (burst mode).
-- � Ensure proper checking of length field errors in received 
--     frames (burst mode).
-- � Ensure invalid frames are dealt with properly and proper 
--     statistics logged (burst mode).
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
--
-- Burst Gigabit Operation:
--  1. In burst mode, receive a proper frame with minimum length plus 
--       extension.  Then receive a frame one byte below minimum length 
--       with bad crc (this is a frame fragment and will not affect 
--       the statistics registers), followed by a good minimum length 
--       frame to finish the burst.
--       Finally receive a good minimum length frame and check the statistics
--  2. In burst mode, receive a proper frame with minimum length plus 
--       extension.  Then receive a proper frame with minimum length 
--       and bad crc (this is will be counted as a crc error), followed
--       by a good minimum length frame to finish the burst.
--       Finally receive a good minimum length frame and check the statistics
--  3. In burst mode, receive a proper frame with minimum length plus 
--       extension, followed by an undersize frame (smaller than 64 bytes) 
--       with good crc, then a good minimum sized frame.
--       Finally, receive a good frame that is minimum size. Check for 
--       undersize frame statistic.
--  4. In burst mode, receive a proper frame with minimum length plus 
--       extension.  Next, receive a jabber (a long frame with bad crc), then
--       a data code error frame (which should be dropper) followed by a 
--       carrier extension code error (the error should be ignored and the 
--       frame transferred to memory as a good frame)
--       Finally receive a good minimum length frame and check the statistics
--  5. Enable length field checking
--       In burst mode, receive a proper frame with minimum length plus 
--       extension. Next, receive a proper sized frame that is 65 bytes in 
--       length with the length field indicating 64 bytes (frame should be
--       reported as error free). Next, receive a proper sized frame that is 
--       64 bytes in length with the length field indicating 65 bytes 
--       (frame should be reported as containing a length error). Finally, 
--       receive a proper sized frame that is 64 bytes in length with the 
--       length field indicating 64 bytes (this frame should be reported as
--       error free).
--       Check for length field error statistic. Ensure frames with length 
--       field errors are discarded.
--  6. In burst mode, receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.  Then, 
--       receive a minimum sized frame that is 63 bytes long with the 
--       length field indicating 64 bytes (the frame should be discarded 
--       and no length error statistic should set).  Finally recieve a good
--       minimum length frame and check the statistics
--  7. In burst mode, receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.  Then, 
--       receive a minimum sized frame with padding with a length field 
--       indicating the length of the frame to the end of the data field and 
--       not include padding.  The frame should be written properly to 
--       memory with no length error statistics set.  Finally receive a 
--       good minimum length frame and check the statistics.
--  8. Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.  Then, receive a maximum 
--       sized frame of 1518 bytes with the length field indicating 1517 (the 
--       actual length is legal and greater than the indicated length, there
--       should be no error generated).  Finally receive a good minimum length 
--       frame and check the statistics.
--  9. Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.  Then, receive a frame 
--       that is 1518 bytes long with the length field indicating 
--       1519 bytes (the actual length < indicated length therfore a length
--       error should be recorded).  Finally receive a good minimum length 
--       frame and check the statistics



-- 10. Enable reception of 1536 byte length frames
--       Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.  Then, receive a maximum 
--       sized frame of 1536 bytes with the length field indicating 1535 (the 
--       actual length is legal and greater than the indicated length, there
--       should be no error generated).  Finally receive a good minimum length 
--       frame and check the statistics.
-- 11. Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.  Then, receive a frame 
--       that is 1536 bytes long with the length field indicating 
--       1537 bytes (the actual length < indicated length therfore a length
--       error should be recorded).  Finally receive a good minimum length 
--       frame and check the statistics
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

